# round 80 (w99): the round-77 cell under the reported five-fold protocol, so the best module form has a fold-ensemble number beside the layer-free 0.920 and the two-family averages. Six gene-protein-reaction redundancy counts appended to the pFBA vector in the affine; folds 0 to 4 at seed 2700. Read fixed here: cv_ensemble_readout.py --prefix w99_pathloggprcv, against w50 (0.920) and the family averages of family_ensembles.py --folds.
ESS_SOLVE_TABLE=/scratch/projects/torchcell-scratch/data/torchcell/reference_flux/ess_solve_encodings_YPD_pfbagpr.npz ESS_ARM=pooled ESS_HIDDEN=12 ESS_HEADS=4 ESS_LAYERS=1 ESS_PREPROC=1 ESS_EPOCHS=200 ESS_BATCH=32 ESS_POSW=1 ESS_SPLIT=ess_fcl_fold0of5_s0.json.gz ESS_SEED=2700 ESS_TAG=_w99pathloggprcv ESS_OUT=w99_pathloggprcv0_h12l1p1_e200_s2700 ESS_EXTRA='--node-embeddings pathways prot_T5_all --ess-readout fba --ess-solve-features pfba --ess-solve-encoding log1p'
